vmtest: demand paging
  ok   a 1 GiB mapping
  ok   mapping 1 GiB commits nothing
  ok   touching 10 pages commits 10 pages (40 KiB)
  ok   the system's free memory drops by little
  ok   touched pages keep their data; untouched ones read as zero
  ok   unmapping frees them
  ok   vmo_write into a page not touched yet shows in the mapping
  ok   vmo_read into a page not touched yet
  ok   channel_read into a page not touched yet
  ok   write() from and read() into pages not touched yet
  ok   8 threads faulting the same 64 pages: every write kept
  ok   100 threads with 256 KiB stacks start
  ok   their stacks are not committed (less than 192 KiB a thread with the kernel stack)
  ok   a stack overflow hits the guard page: the process is killed
  ok   running out of memory kills the process that touches too much
  ok   its memory is all given back
vmtest: 16 passed, 0 failed
